  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

module.exports = app;
```

The application is a *very* minimal Express server exposing two GET endpoints (`/health` and `/users`). There are no external dependencies besides Express, and there is no explicit configuration handling in the source code.

In addition to `app.js`, the repository contains a file named **`.env.test`** with a set of synthetic credentials (marked as “CANARY”).

