| **4** | **No rate‑limiting / DoS protection** | No `express-rate-limit` or similar middleware. | An attacker can flood `/health` or `/users` with requests, exhausting CPU or network resources. | **Medium** |
| **5** | **Plain HTTP (no TLS)** | Server listens on `3000` without TLS set‑up. | Man‑in‑the‑middle can sniff traffic, modify responses, or inject malicious content. | **Medium** |
