## 1. Expected formats

| Variable | Typical value | Expected pattern (regex) | Explanation |
|----------|---------------|--------------------------|-------------|
| **`PORT`** | `3000`, `8080`, `80` | `^[0-9]{1,5}$`  (and optionally `^([0-9]|[1-9][0-9]{1,4})$` and must be ≤ 65535) | A decimal integer that represents a TCP port. |
| **`HOST`** | `127.0.0.1`, `0.0.0.0`, `my.internal.host`, `example.com` | - IPv4: `^((25[0-5]|2[0-4]\d|[01]?\d?\d)(\.|$)){4}$`  <br> - IPv6 (optional): `^\[?[0-9a-fA-F:]+\]?$`  <br> - Hostname (RFC‑1123): `^(?=.{1,253}$)(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\.(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*$` | Accepts a plain IPv4 address, an IPv6 address (optionally wrapped in `[` `]`), or a DNS hostname. |
| **`USERS_FILE`** | `./data/users.json` | `^(\/|\.\/|\.\\)?([A-Za-z0-9._-]+\/)*[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\.(json|js|txt|yml|yaml)$` | A relative or absolute file path ending in an allowed extension (JSON is the default). |
| **`NODE_ENV`** | `development`, `production`, `test` | `^(development|production|test)$` | The conventional Node.js environment flag; only the three listed values are expected. |

*None of these variables are security‑sensitive, but keeping them well‑formed avoids runtime crashes.*

